#Largest Element in an Array

##Problem Statement
to find the largest element in the given array.

##Approach 
traverse the array elements one-by-one and find the largest element.

##Algorithm
1. Start
2. Read an array with it's elements.
3. Consider the max = arr[0]
4. Traverse the array from index : i=0 ti (n-1).
5. Apply the conditions : if(max < arr[i]) then put max = arr[i]
6. Return arr[i] is the largest. 
7. Return -1 in case the element is not in the array.
8. Exit.

##C++ Implementation
#include<iostream>
using namespace std;
void largestarr(int *arr, int n){
int max = arr[0];
for(int i = 0; i<n; i++){
if(max < arr[i]){
    max = arr[i];
    return max;
    }
}
return -1;
}

int main(){
int arr[] = {2,4,7,8,10};
int n = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(int);
int max = largestarr(arr, n);
cout << "the largest element in the array is: "<< max;                            // output : 10
cout << endl;
return 0;
}


Time Complexity : 0(n)
Space Complexity : 0(1)
